{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
  "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress uses ordinary words in the statute, those words should get their ordinary meaning. In SORNA, the Sex Offender Registration and Notification Act, Congress did use ordinary words, and it used them in an ordinary way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Mr. Rothfeld, I wondered if I could ask you about three interrelated points concerning your textual argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, I think that the ordinary assumption is that when the present tense is used in a statute that's creating a criminal offense, it refers to conduct that takes place after the statute was enacted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Rothfeld, would you clarify one thing? You\u2019re not questioning the Attorney General's determination that the underlying sex offense can have occurred pre-SORNA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And do -- do they generally require registration even if the offense was committed before the registration act was passed in the State?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Would you say this at the moment -- you may not know, but I think it would be helpful. At the time this was passed, would you say almost all States had some kind of registration act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: And would that be the case after SORNA, that some States would have less extensive coverage than others?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, what about going back to the purpose? There's a section on page 26 of the House report where they go in some length to saying that the purpose is this is going to help with 100,000 missing people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GANNON: Well, it -- it first of all imposes a Federal registration requirement. So in --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Okay. So Congress passes this statute. And how does it help specifically with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress considered that type of regime as being inadequate. Congress obviously thought that the State violations that were occurring with 100,000 sex offenders who had eluded registration, gone underground, was a problem they wanted to solve."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0273efe9385e019c653995a0116a2becbb2f0aee709aa8102f038ec12f1e1607",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0273efe9385e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GANNON: I think that lots of jurisdictional hooks referring to travel and interstate commerce are phrased in present tense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1301",
      "confidence": 0.0,
